# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) to override for your own machine.
#
# VITE_API_BASE is where the client sends every request. It is read at BUILD
# time, not at runtime - Vite inlines it - so changing it means rebuilding.
#
# Leave it unset for the two arrangements that already work without it:
#
#   * dev      - vite.config.ts proxies /api to 127.0.0.1:8000
#   * one host - the API serves the build from the same origin (see Dockerfile)
#
# Set it only when the client is hosted somewhere the API is not, in which case
# the API also needs DETOURA_CORS_ORIGINS set to this client's origin.
#
# VITE_API_BASE=https://api.detoura.app/api/v1

# VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER picks the analytics backend (src/lib/analytics.ts).
# Leave it unset for local dev and any deploy that doesn't need analytics -
# track() is then a no-op: no script tag, no cookie, no network request.
#
#   ga4        - loads Google's gtag.js. Also set VITE_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID.
#   plausible  - loads Plausible's script. Optionally set
#                VITE_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN (defaults to the page's own hostname).
#
# Either script is lazy-loaded only when its provider is selected here - never
# by default, and never for a build that leaves this unset.
#
# VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=ga4
# VITE_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX
# VITE_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=detoura.app

# VITE_SENTRY_DSN would enable error reporting (src/lib/errorTracking.ts).
# Unset by default, which keeps captureException() logging to the console with
# zero Sentry dependency and zero network calls - there is no @sentry/* package
# in this project yet, so setting this today only turns on a dev-time warning,
# not a real integration (see the TODO in that file).
#
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0
